077, "excludes_null": false, "dysregulation_hr": 1.2879, "dysregulation_ci_low": 1.2391, "dysregulation_ci_high": 1.3387, "c_baseline": 0.7394, "c_clock": 0.7408, "c_dysregulation": 0.7567, "c_joint": 0.7573, "dysregulation_adds_p": 4.023575258321898e-27, "clock_adds_p": 0.05873423151450893}, {"clock": "SkinBloodAge", "predicts": "chronological_age", "note": "Horvath 2018 skin-and-blood clock.", "hr_alone": 1.0562, "hr": 1.0485, "ci_low": 0.9922, "ci_high": 1.108, "excludes_null": false, "dysregulation_hr": 1.2907, "dysregulation_ci_low": 1.2419, "dysregulation_ci_high": 1.3415, "c_baseline": 0.7394, "c_clock": 0.7401, "c_dysregulation": 0.7567, "c_joint": 0.7571, "dysregulation_adds_p": 1.3717173498758641e-27, "clock_adds_p": 0.08673393381147612}, {"clock": "WeidnerAge", "predicts": "chronological_age", "note": "Weidner 2014 three-CpG age predictor.", "hr_alone": 1.0441, "hr": 1.0256, "ci_low": 0.9762, "ci_high": 1.0775, "excludes_null": false, "dysregulation_hr": 1.2885, "dysregulation_ci_low": 1.2397, "dysregulation_ci_high": 1.3392, "c_baseline": 0.7394, "c_clock": 0.74, "c_dysregulation": 0.7567, "c_joint": 0.7568, "dysregulation_adds_p": 2.188401978875554e-27, "clock_adds_p": 0.3162816982425135}], "caveats": ["Age floor of 50: the DNAm subsample is adults 50+, so the age range is 50-85 rather than the 20-80 of the 2017-2018 cohort. The critical-slowing-down design loses roughly half its dynamic range; any CSD estimate here is less powered than the published one, not more.", "Age is topcoded at 85.", "CRP is the standard assay in mg/dL (converted to mg/L here), not the high-sensitivity assay used in 2017-2018. Detection limits differ at the low end.", "Public-use mortality records are perturbed by NCHS: a subset carry synthetic follow-up time or cause of death. Aggregate estimates are designed to survive this; individual records are not trustworthy on their own.", "Survey weights (WTMEC4YR, WTDN4YR) and the design variables (SDMVPSU, SDMVSTRA) are carried but NOT applied by default; unweighted estimates are not nationally representative.", "Clocks are NCHS's own computed values, not recomputed here. That removes our normalization from the picture and also means we cannot audit it.", "Cross-sectional exposure: markers and methylation are measured once, at baseline. Only the outcome is longitudinal."]}